+# kind: EA_LOG
+# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
+# XEMA CONFORMANCE FIXTURE — EA_LOG (authoritative). This is the fixture that lets
+# `--verify` reach a true PASS. Produce it like this:
+#
+#   1. Attach SimpleEA (PRESET_XEMA) in the MT5 Strategy Tester.
+#   2. Use the DEFAULT XEMA config (do NOT apply any per-pair findings). The
+#      harness default config must match: EMA 20/50, dual HTF M15+H1 EMA20/50,
+#      ADX p50 lb100, all other voters OFF, SL swing lb20, BE 2R, LPR 3R->2R/4R->3R.
+#   3. Pick a SHORT window (e.g. EURUSD H1, 1–2 months) so the fixture is small.
+#   4. Turn on trade logging (collect/log mode / DebugFlow) and run the test.
+#   5. Export each executed trade as one row below, in DATA-CLOCK bar time.
+#
+# Columns (header row required; this comment block is ignored by the loader):
+#   entry_time  : 'YYYY.MM.DD HH:MM'  bar time of the entry SIGNAL bar (the closed
+#                 bar whose cross fired; entry fills next-bar open — the harness
+#                 matches on the signal bar, tolerance ±1 bar).
+#   direction   : BUY | SELL   (or +1 / -1)
+#   sl          : initial stop-loss PRICE placed at entry (5 decimals FX / 3 JPY).
+#   exit_time   : 'YYYY.MM.DD HH:MM'  bar time the position closed.
+#   exit_reason : SL | REVCROSS | BE | LPR   (BE/SL-at-BE and LPR/TRAIL are treated
+#                 as soft-equivalent by --verify).
+#
+# Then verify (from the harness dir), pointing --htf at the real M15 file so the
+# M15 HTF is reconstructed from actual M15 bars (an H1 CSV alone cannot do this):
+#
+#   python3 xema_harness_260902-01.py <EURUSD_H1_file>.csv \
+#       --htf M15=<EURUSD_M15_file>.csv \
+#       --verify fixtures/conformance_EURUSD_H1_<dates>.csv
+#
+# Expected: CONFORMANCE PASS, exit code 0. If FAIL, read the printed per-bar diff:
+# either the EA changed since HEAD b0244b7 (re-derive the harness) or the harness
+# drifted (fix + re-verify). Do NOT trust sweep output until this PASSes.
+#
+# If you can only produce a SignalScan/DebugFlow dump of a handful of bars (no full
+# trade log), save it with `# kind: SIGNALSCAN`, fill entry_time+direction (+sl if
+# available), leave exit columns blank, and --verify will report PARTIAL.
+# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
+entry_time,direction,sl,exit_time,exit_reason
